{
 "description": "Facet-payload validation and fail-closed rules (D10; backlog #17 - run 1's Blocker P9-1). A stdlib facet payload MUST validate against the normative descriptor schema; a non-stdlib facet MUST be pinned in the bundle manifest (its stub schema then governs) or carry the private: prefix (ignored by definition); anything else is unregistered - dangerous-by-default, a validation error. The adversarial cases below are the P9-1 probes, now permanent. method-vectors (backlog #55, 2026-11-14): an Assessment's `method` is a facet payload. Its keys are facet ids, resolved as the keys of `facets` are - the standard library, then the schemas the bundle pins, then `private:`, else an error - and each payload is held to its schema. `expected-errors` is the number of errors for the object. Each of `expected-frags` must occur in some error: an error about a method names it as method '<key>', one about a facet as facet '<key>'. The name of a vector is no part of an error.",
 "vectors": [
  {
   "name": "stdlib-payload-valid",
   "object": {
    "id": "https://ex.org/req/1",
    "version": "1",
    "lifecycle": "active",
